{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"highborn-gabardine-dairycow","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Proposal (operator-adjudicated — filed from measurement 50e3-6d2a, not implemented)\n\nThe measurement on 50e3-6d2a-0e7f-4e92 found the 88 recorded caused_by edges cannot be\npartitioned into blame-derived guesses vs explicitly supplied attributions: `_apply_caused_by`\n(src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py) writes both through `_write_link_event` with no\nprovenance field. Consequences measured there:\n\n- The population study could only BOUND the derived share (38 consistent-with-blame / 6\n  divergent / 44 not reproducible today).\n- On the only 8 edges with independently proven origins, the deriver scored 0 correct,\n  1 confidently wrong (named the innocent producer), 7 abstained — yet on read a guessed edge\n  is indistinguishable from those proven ones, so escape-rate lenses and the epic-close\n  caused_by floor weight them identically.\n\n## Proposed change (small, schema-level)\n\nAdd a `derived: blame | explicit` (or equivalent) field to the caused_by LINK event at the two\nwrite sites in transition_close.py, defaulting old events to unknown on read. Consumers\n(`rebar metrics` escape-rate lenses) may then report supplied vs derived rates separately or\ndiscount derived edges. NO change to the deriver's fail-closed behaviour is proposed — the\nmeasurement found the strict-majority abstention is working as designed.\n\n## Why filed, not done\n\nSchema/gate-adjacent changes are operator-adjudicated per project policy. This ticket is the\nproposal; the evidence base is the findings comment on 50e3-6d2a-0e7f-4e92.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Operator decision recorded on this ticket (accept/reject/amend the marker design).\n- [ ] If accepted: link event schema carries the marker, both write sites populate it, old\n      events read as unknown, and docs/event-schema.md documents it.\n- [ ] If accepted: rebar metrics distinguishes supplied vs derived caused_by edges in at least\n      the escape-rate lens.","id":"6536-367c-e358-424d","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Proposal: provenance marker (derived vs explicit) on caused_by link events"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787395166332595001,"uuid":"5fbd2a24-89f5-415c-aae1-2ed7559ecd61"}